    "reasoning": "Fe(III)dicitrate names a two-citrate coordination species, whereas ferric citrate CHEBI:144421 contains one citrate; CHEBI:4991 is iron(3+) dicitrate(3-). The MediaDB mnemonic KEGG:fe3dcit is not a verified KEGG compound accession. Diverse recipe occurrences and literature leads do not identify counterions or prove that a dicitrate reagent was weighed. Direct inspection of Lovley1988 p1473 specifies Fe(III)-citrate20mM, without dicitrate or supplier form. This corroborates a ferric-citrate material but does not establish the2:1 ligand species asserted by the shared MediaDB mnemonic; other source papers have distinct contexts.",
